                             "translated":  false,
                             "text_used":  "On date 15 June 2026 at time 14:30 UTC, person Colonel James Carter, holding the rank of Colonel and of nationality American, reported to organization Joint Task Force Sentinel. The military unit 3rd Armored Brigade was deployed as part of operation name Operation Iron Shield.\n\nThe unit moved from location Fort Eagle Base toward Sector Delta at coordinates 34.0522°N, 118.2437°W. During the mission, a vehicle M2 Bradley Infantry Fighting Vehicle escorted a weapon system HIMARS launcher carrying precision-guided munitions.\n\nAir support was provided by the aircraft F-35 Lightning II operating under communication identifier EAGLE-21. Maritime surveillance was conducted by the vessel USS Arlington positioned offshore. Ground troops utilized equipment AN/PRC-158 tactical radios and advanced night-vision systems.\n\nThe convoy arrived at facility Forward Operating Base Falcon, where commanders monitored an event involving unauthorized drone activity near the perimeter. Intelligence updates were transmitted through communication identifier ALPHA-NET-07 and coordinated with allied forces.\n\nFollowing successful reconnaissance and threat assessment, the military unit secured the objective area without casualties. The organization Joint Task Force Sentinel declared operation name Operation Iron Shield a success and scheduled a follow-up event for 18 June 2026 at 09:00 UTC.",
                             "original_text":  "On date 15 June 2026 at time 14:30 UTC, person Colonel James Carter, holding the rank of Colonel and of nationality American, reported to organization Joint Task Force Sentinel. The military unit 3rd Armored Brigade was deployed as part of operation name Operation Iron Shield.\n\nThe unit moved from location Fort Eagle Base toward Sector Delta at coordinates 34.0522°N, 118.2437°W. During the mission, a vehicle M2 Bradley Infantry Fighting Vehicle escorted a weapon system HIMARS launcher carrying precision-guided munitions.\n\nAir support was provided by the aircraft F-35 Lightning II operating under communication identifier EAGLE-21. Maritime surveillance was conducted by the vessel USS Arlington positioned offshore. Ground troops utilized equipment AN/PRC-158 tactical radios and advanced night-vision systems.\n\nThe convoy arrived at facility Forward Operating Base Falcon, where commanders monitored an event involving unauthorized drone activity near the perimeter. Intelligence updates were transmitted through communication identifier ALPHA-NET-07 and coordinated with allied forces.\n\nFollowing successful reconnaissance and threat assessment, the military unit secured the objective area without casualties. The organization Joint Task Force Sentinel declared operation name Operation Iron Shield a success and scheduled a follow-up event for 18 June 2026 at 09:00 UTC.",
